Fase: navegacao. COOP/COEP sem troca de processo nao derruba o Firefox.
Arquivo: dom/base/Document.cpp
web.whatsapp.com manda Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin +
Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp. O Gecko normal abre um
BrowsingContext novo em outro processo; no SODOS (processo unico) o mesmo
contexto tentava virar REQUIRE_CORP, CanSet(OpenerPolicy) recusava e
Transaction::Commit dava MOZ_CRASH "CanSet failed for field(s): OpenerPolicy"
(#PF escrevendo em 0, CRASH.LOG em FIREFOX.EXE+0x5DD4611).
Agora a politica cai para same-origin (sem crossOriginIsolated).
Teste: abrir https://web.whatsapp.com e navegar dele para outro site.

--- a/dom/base/Document.cpp
+++ b/dom/base/Document.cpp
@@ -3527,6 +3527,23 @@
       docShell->GetBrowsingContext()) {
     CheckIsBadPolicy(policy, docShell->GetBrowsingContext(), aChannel);
 
+#if defined(__SODOS__)
+    // SODOS roda em um processo so: o Gecko nao troca o BrowsingContext
+    // quando a pagina pede isolamento (COOP same-origin + COEP require-corp,
+    // ex. web.whatsapp.com), e CanSet(OpenerPolicy) recusa entrar ou sair de
+    // REQUIRE_CORP no mesmo contexto -> MOZ_CRASH "CanSet failed" em
+    // Transaction::Commit. Fica sem crossOriginIsolated, mas nao derruba.
+    {
+      auto requireCORP =
+          nsILoadInfo::OPENER_POLICY_SAME_ORIGIN_EMBEDDER_POLICY_REQUIRE_CORP;
+      auto cur = docShell->GetBrowsingContext()->GetOpenerPolicy();
+      if (cur != policy && (cur == requireCORP || policy == requireCORP)) {
+        policy = cur == requireCORP ? cur
+                                    : nsILoadInfo::OPENER_POLICY_SAME_ORIGIN;
+      }
+    }
+#endif
+
     // Setting the opener policy on a discarded context has no effect.
     (void)docShell->GetBrowsingContext()->SetOpenerPolicy(policy);
   }
